  "review": {
    "label": "curated_editorial",
    "look_ahead": "Jim Goodwin would take the club into 2022-23, then be dismissed in January with Barry Robson producing a third-place finish.\n",
    "read": "The Glass experiment is the record's clearest warning against reading a single season as a verdict. The club tried to change how it played and where it recruited, and the league results fell sharply. The next two seasons test whether that was a transition cost or a structural mistake.\n",
    "trade_off": "A change of direction can cost league position before it produces a new baseline. The season is evidence of the cost; it is not by itself evidence that the direction was wrong.\n",
    "what_did_not": "The league fell from fourth to tenth, the League Cup ended in the second round and the Scottish Cup ended in the fifth. The summer rebuild did not produce a settled team.\n",
    "what_worked": "The club changed manager in February and finished 10th on 41 points, in the bottom six. The European campaign reached the play-off round, one round beyond the previous season's third qualifying round.\n"
  },
